  "method": {
    "art": "Approved campus/academic87-2 originals copied byte for byte; other4base,6winter maps and2five-crop tree-removal atlases generated with image_gen. Only local geometric registration used for sports winter oval.",
    "mask": "Mask first: independent image-generated transparent oak cutouts used as semantic selection references, aligned back to each source crop by SIFT/RANSAC; union with current main oakl semantic prior, map-edge cleanup, connected-component selection and filled holes. Conservative watercolor/snow fringe margin included. Final alpha strictly0/255; final tree RGB is always selected from the fixed source map, not from the reference cutout.",
    "assembly": "Tree layer RGB selected from fixed original map by mask. Image-generated tree-removal patch changes nooak map only inside mask. Recomposition pixel-identical.",
    "coordinates": "pixel_box=[left,top,right,bottom] exclusive end; pivot/acorns/drop are full1024x1536 canvas pixels; tap=[x%,y%,radius%] radius based on map width.",
    "legacy_oakp_note": "Current main oakp is a background replacement patch with asymmetric surrounding context, not the tree cutout. Requested center difference is relative to that placed patch rectangle. Actual tree placement is also compared with main oakl rectangle separately.",
    "selection_box_note": "pixel_box bounds the conservative binary selection and includes a small surrounding fringe. Main oakp is a background replacement patch, so its center differs from the actual oakl tree rectangle; both differences are recorded. Source tree pixels and original pivot positions are never moved.",
    "preview_rotation": "Full tree layer rotated around original game pivot by+2degrees for preview; -2degrees also inspected. Preview interpolation can be soft, original layers remain binary.",
    "phone_preview": "True412px-wide maps arranged3+2 to satisfy1600px maximum; five in one row at412px would require2060px before spacing."
  },
